  "note": "Nominations were announced by V. M. Conran, town clerk, at Armagh City Hall on Wednesday 4 May: eighteen candidates for the twenty seats, so there was no contest in any ward. Only two candidates, J. O'Neill and F. McKee, both Independents, were nominated for the ward's four seats; P. O'Brien and P. McSorley, who had sat as Independent Labour members of the old council, were \"deemed to be returned unopposed\" as outgoing councillors. Polling day for the urban councils was Wednesday 18 May 1949 (Belfast News-Letter, 19 May 1949, p. 5: \"Polling took place yesterday for the election of county borough, borough and urban councils in Ulster\")."
